  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1250 AM EST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\n- Only Minor Travel Impacts through the Weekend\n\nA full latitude trough across the central CONUS cuts off from the\nnorthern stream with the upper low and large sfc cyclone tapping \nboth Gulf and Atlantic moisture as it moves northeast up the \nAppalachians by the end of the week. The northwest precip shield, \nassociated with an area of mid level frontogenesis, will bring \nrain moving in from the south this afternoon and evening with the\npotential for some wet snow mixing in late tonight and Friday \nmorning.\n\nSince the low is cut off from the northern stream, there is a \nlimited push of cold air with surface temperatures near or above\nfreezing during the bulk of the precip. Model soundings from the\nGFS show the wet bulb zero height near the surface late tonight \ninto Friday morning, and there could be some minor impacts to \ntravel if wet snow is heavy enough to accumulate on roads.\n\nThe precip winds down on Friday as the trowal/mid-level f-gen \ntranslates east and is replaced by shortwave ridging before a \nnorthern stream shortwave trough arrives late in the weekend. Cold\nair is once again limited but wet snow could mix in by Sunday\nnight across the northern forecast area.",
